    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d72">

                <pb facs="0218" n="126" xml:id="pg126"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/8918a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d72-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-18T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 18, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6611. Department has received through the Greek Legation an intimation from
                    Venizelos of the desirability of the Allies issuing some statement indicating
                    their intention to stand behind Greece and see that her rights are protected,
                    and at the same time conveying an expression of their appreciation of Greece’s
                    entry into the war on the side of the Allies. The Department desires to know
                    whether the British Government has received a similar message and if so intends
                    to make any such declaration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d72-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d72-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, on the same date, to the
                    Ambassador in France (No. 3199).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
